+
+## NPC knowledge provenance
+
+Knowledge is not global merely because a fact exists in continuity state.
+
+For every positive knowledge state (`partial`, `suspects`, `knows`, `false_belief`),
+`rp_stage_turn.knowledge[]` must include a source with one of:
+
+- `user_asserted` — the current explicit user turn establishes the character knows it;
+- `observed` — the character actually perceives the evidence in the current/accepted story;
+- `told_by` — another character/source told them; provide `source.reference`;
+- `public` — the information is already established as public;
+- `inferred` — inference only, which may support `suspects`/`partial`, not direct `knows`;
+- `existing` — reuse of a matching accepted prior knowledge row.
+
+When a **newly introduced NPC** mentions, pursues, or acts on an already accepted fact,
+include that fact id in `npc_updates[].knowledge_refs` and bind a matching
+`knowledge[].fact_id` with explicit provenance in the same stage. If there is no valid
+source, the NPC must remain ignorant of that fact.
+
+## Retraction cascade
+
+If the current user explicitly corrects an accepted prior **story turn as never having
+happened**, call `rp_stage_turn` with `retract_turns` and `retraction_reason` (normally
+`advances_story=false`). The native runtime removes continuity records originating in
+those turns instead of leaving ghost Canon behind. This includes facts, knowledge,
+events, commitments, threads, agendas, recent beats, and NPC runtime updates from the
+retracted turn.
+
+Use `facts.supersedes` instead when only one fact is wrong and the rest of that prior
+turn remains valid. Do not use event `status=cancelled` as a substitute for retracting
+a beat the user says never happened.
+
