+### Retractions
+
+`retract_turns` + `retraction_reason` is the whole-beat correction path when the
+current explicit user says an accepted prior story turn never happened. It cascades
+removal of continuity records originating in the target turn(s): facts, knowledge,
+events, commitments, threads, agendas, recent beats, and NPC runtime updates. A small
+retraction audit record remains so recall can avoid resurrecting the invalid beat.
+
+Use `facts.supersedes` for a targeted fact correction when the rest of the prior turn
+remains valid. Event `cancelled` by itself is not a historical rollback.
 
